$F668 b KindRecords 8 ; The kind records: 11 bytes, or 7 for a kind that never switches
> KindTable points to each. +0 the width, +1 the height (record +7, +8); +2 bits 6-7 into the record's +0 (bit 6 deadly to Rick and the enemies, bit 7 the detonator test), bits 0-5 x 4 the behaviour after the switch (record +$15); +3/+4 the path, +5/+6 the animation; +7/+8 the second path, +9/+10 the second animation (SwitchTrapPath $A4D5 swaps them in). A record followed 7 bytes later by the next one has no second half of its own: its +7..+10 are the next record's first bytes, which no switch reads for such a kind (or the switch would take them).
