@module kinds ; The trap kinds: the kind table, the animation scripts, the paths and the kind records
$F3DB w KindTable 8 ; A word a kind (0-45): the address of its record
> LevelHeader+0 points here. SpawnMapObject $9D6C takes the word at KindTable + 2 x the map entry's kind (below $74) for a trap or pickup. Kind 0 is never used (its word is $0000); kinds 5, 12, 14, 15, 16 have records but no map entry uses them.
@res level/kinds.bin
$F437 b TrapAnims 8 ; The animation scripts of the trap kinds
> Read by AnimateTrap $A608 from a record's +$0A/+$0B: a byte below $80 is a frame (SpriteFrameMap: the sprite, bit 7 mirrored; frame $7F hides the object) shown one pass; $80 + n then a frame: that frame for n more passes; $FD n plays effect n; $FF and a word jumps there (every script ends in one). A kind record gives the first script (+5/+6) and the one after the switch (+9/+10).
@res level/anims.bin
$F437 ; kind 1
$F43C ; kinds 6, 12, 23, 28, 28 (second), 33, 33 (second), 41, 44, 45
$F441 ; kinds 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 14, 15, 16, 17, 24
$F445 ; kinds 4 (second), 9 (second), 14 (second), 17 (second)
$F44C ; kinds 5 (second), 7 (second), 8 (second), 15 (second), 16 (second)
$F453 ; kinds 10, 11, 20
$F457 ; kind 10 (second)
$F464 ; kind 11 (second)
$F471 ; kind 13
$F481 ; kinds 18, 43
$F485 ; kinds 18 (second), 43 (second)
$F492 ; kinds 19, 19 (second), 25, 25 (second), 40
$F497 ; kind 20 (second)
$F4A4 ; kind 21
$F4AA ; kinds 13 (second), 35 (second)
