@module kinds ; The trap kinds: the kind table, the animation scripts, the paths and the kind records
$F22D w KindTable 8 ; A word a kind (0-68): the address of its record
> LevelHeader+0 points here. SpawnMapObject $9D6C takes the word at KindTable + 2 x the map entry's kind (below $74) for a trap or pickup. Kind 0 is never used (its word is $0001); kinds 13, 16, 24, 25, 28, 29, 49, 50, 52 have records but no map entry uses them.
@res level/kinds.bin
$F2B7 b TrapAnims 8 ; The animation scripts of the trap kinds
> Read by AnimateTrap $A608 from a record's +$0A/+$0B: a byte below $80 is a frame (SpriteFrameMap: the sprite, bit 7 mirrored; frame $7F hides the object) shown one pass; $80 + n then a frame: that frame for n more passes; $FD n plays effect n; $FF and a word jumps there (every script ends in one). A kind record gives the first script (+5/+6) and the one after the switch (+9/+10).
@res level/anims.bin
$F2B7 ; kinds 14, 21
$F2BB ; kind 1
$F2C1 ; kind 1 (second)
$F2C8 ; kind 2
$F2CD ; kinds 44, 68
$F2D1 ; kinds 3, 9, 42, 43, 44 (second), 68 (second)
