$F64D b TrapPaths 8 ; The paths of the trap kinds
> Read by UpdateTrap $A2F7 from a record's +$0F/+$10: pairs of a count and a step (the high nibble the x step, the low nibble the y step, each signed, 7 meaning 8 pixels) applied once a pass count times; $FF n plays effect n; 0 and a word jumps there (the loop point: a one-shot trap ends there, a waiting trap switches to its second path). A kind record gives the first path (+3/+4) and the second (+7/+8).
@res level/paths.bin
