@module kinds ; The trap kinds: the kind table, the animation scripts, the paths and the kind records
$F1CB w KindTable 8 ; A word a kind (0-54): the address of its record
> LevelHeader+0 points here. SpawnMapObject $9D6C takes the word at KindTable + 2 x the map entry's kind (below $74) for a trap or pickup. Kind 0 is never used (its word is $0041); kinds 4, 14, 35, 37 have records but no map entry uses them.
@res level/kinds.bin
$F239 b TrapAnims 8 ; The animation scripts of the trap kinds
> Read by AnimateTrap $A608 from a record's +$0A/+$0B: a byte below $80 is a frame (SpriteFrameMap: the sprite, bit 7 mirrored; frame $7F hides the object) shown one pass; $80 + n then a frame: that frame for n more passes; $FD n plays effect n; $FF and a word jumps there (every script ends in one). A kind record gives the first script (+5/+6) and the one after the switch (+9/+10).
@res level/anims.bin
$F239 ; kind 8
$F23D ; kind 1
$F244 ; kinds 2, 2 (second), 4, 4 (second), 15, 15 (second), 24, 24 (second), 28, 28 (second), 32, 36, 36 (second), 38, 38 (second)
